   147	machine's numerical stack, each with exactly the binding recomputed now. If
   148	the pod gate fails, the run stops and is reported; the frozen estimates stay primary.
   149	
   150	## 6. Cost and spending controls
   151	
   152	`python3 docs/revision/followup2/cost_estimate.py`: up to 29.48 core-hours, 3.18 USD at 0.108 USD per core-hour (19 cells x
   153	3 rounds priced as registered doubling checks plus a held-out evaluation each round); the gate cells run serially, 1.06
   154	hours; billed path 3.60 hours (gate, an X7-SC cell's three rounds with 16 workers starting the 9 X7-SC cells first, 0.3 h
   155	preparation and tail) = 2.01 USD at 0.56 USD per hour. Estimate 3.30 USD (x 1.25 = 4.12); **stop cap
   156	4.25 USD**; **reservation 5.525 USD** (1.3 x the stop cap, the watchdog bound; amendment above) in ledger category `followup`
   157	(cap 72 USD shared by all follow-up runs; `budget_followup.py reserve`). A paid run requires `--started-at <allocation time>`, a positive rate, and the launcher's attempts file
   158	(`--attempts`). Admission is checked before each gate cell and before every round of every
   159	cell, including its first, with the round's estimate plus its evaluation and a 0.1-hour shutdown allowance; a running round
   160	is never killed (author's instruction). A cell refused admission, or stopped by it after a completed round, keeps its frozen estimate as primary and is
   161	reported "stopped at the cost cap"; any partial result is kept under `partial` and never substituted; after the last running round finishes, the pod is deleted and verified. This is an admission limit, not a
   162	billing ceiling.
   163	
   164	**Launcher handoff (draft 5).** The launcher copy pushes to the pod, before every paid driver call, its current
   165	`<name>.attempts` file and the ledger, and passes `--attempts`, `--ledger`, `--run-tag`, `--started-at` (the current pod's
   166	allocation time), `--usd-per-hour` (the price ceiling MAXCPH), `--stop-file /root/STOP`, and `--soft-deadline` (its soft
   167	deadline). The driver reads the launcher's own event lines (`<pod> <epoch> start`, `<pod> <epoch> deleted`;
   168	`guards.attempts_spend`): each closed attempt counts at the ceiling, and the open start is the current pod, counted from
   169	its recorded `start` event (a later `--started-at` cannot shorten it; it must lie between that event and now); malformed or unordered lines are refused (tests with lines in the launcher's exact format); spend of
   170	earlier launches comes from the ledger rows tagged with the run tag, since the launcher truncates its file per launch. The
   171	driver checks the STOP file and the soft deadline before each gate cell and before every round of every cell, so it
   172	honours the launcher's between-stage stop without a mid-round stop (test).
   173	
   174	**Admission before every paid step (draft 6).** Before the pod's first paid step, and before each later one (the reset
   175	reproduction gate included), the launcher runs `python3 docs/revision/followup2/guards.py admit --cap-usd 4.25
   176	--usd-per-hour <ceiling> --started-at <allocation> --attempts <file> --ledger <ledger> --run-tag convergence --hours <step estimate>
   177	--stop-file /root/STOP --soft-deadline <soft>` and starts the step only on exit 0. Reservation: `python3 docs/revision/followup/budget_followup.py --reserve convergence-<n> 4.42`; the
   178	launcher requires one `followup` reservation `convergence-<n>` (its launch tag) of at least 1.3 x the stop cap minus the run's
   179	recorded spend (5.525 USD on a first launch; the ledger grants less when the category is nearly full), else no pod; the reservation covers the watchdog bound, 1.3 x the stop cap, because a stage admitted within the cap finishes and only the watchdog at 1.3 x the cap stops a running stage (churn launcher review r1, Sol and Astra); `guards.check_grant` against the stop cap is replaced by the launcher's check that one `followup` reservation tagged with this launch covers 1.3 x the stop cap minus the run's recorded spend. The launcher copy itself (a copy of `results/pods/reset_pod.sh`) is not part
   180	of this folder and is to be written and tested offline before allocation.
   181	
   182	**Launcher and the cap.** The pod launcher is a copy of `results/pods/reset_pod.sh` with `results/pods/podctl.py`. Its soft
   183	deadline is the cap at the price ceiling MAXCPH, counted from the first creation request of the launch, so it holds across
   184	attempts; at the soft deadline the remote script stops before its next stage (a STOP file read between stages), and the
   185	driver's own admission check (`--cap-usd`, `--started-at`, `--attempts`) stops between stages or rounds as well. A running
   186	stage is never stopped (the author: do not kill jobs). The single exception is the watchdog, which deletes the pod at 1.3 x
   187	the cap at the price ceiling; that is the only mid-stage stop. Closed attempts are listed in the launcher's
   188	`<name>.attempts` file (event lines `<pod> <epoch> start` and `<pod> <epoch> deleted`), which the driver reads
   189	(`guards.attempts_spend`) and counts toward the
   190	cap before each paid attempt; a paid run without it is refused (no default of zero); after the launch the spend is recorded
   191	in the ledger (`budget_v2.py --record`).
   192	
   193	## 7. Steps
   194	
   195	1. Internal review to consensus; freeze the plan; save the Mac gate evidence.
   196	2. Reserve 5.525 USD in the ledger (input 4.42); one pod: the gate with `--site pod`, then `convergence_v2.py --workers 16 --evidence
   197	   <four gate records> --cap-usd 4.25 --started-at T --attempts A --ledger L --run-tag convergence --stop-file /root/STOP --soft-deadline S`; delete and verify; record the spend.
