- 2026-11-13, Run B bundle: a one-line move-then-copy script went on after the move to the Trash failed (an empty
  target from a failed `mkdir`), so `cp` overwrote the old Mac gate records in place. Nothing was lost (copies are in
  `f2_bundle_a.tgz`). Guard: `results/pods/trash.sh` (copy in `docs/revision/followup/`) fails on no paths, a missing
  path or a failed move (negative tests run 2026-11-13); every replace is `trash.sh OLD && cp NEW`.

- 2026-11-13, Run A: the launcher verifies the pulled inventories only after RUN OK, so a run that ends "STOPPED BEFORE"
  comes back unchecked. Run A's records were then checked by hand with the launcher's own `verify` body (161 + 27, 0 bad).
  Guard (written rule, launcher frozen while Run B runs): after any pod end other than RUN OK, run
  `sed -n '86,96p' followup2_pod.sh > verify_inv.py; python3 verify_inv.py <dir>` on every output directory before any
  analysis; fix in the launcher before its next use (verify on every end state that pulled records).

- 2026-11-13, Run B: `convergence_v2.py` collects every cell with `list(ex.map(...))` and writes results only after all
  cells end, so one worker killed with signal 9 (likely out of memory: 16 workers, 29 GB) lost 3.6 h of work and about
  3.43 USD. Three review rounds missed it; no test killed a worker, and no step measured memory per worker. Guard (for
  the rerun, tests first): a test that kills one worker and checks that finished cells are on disk and skipped on resume;
  a Mac-measured peak memory per cell that sets the worker count, checked by the launcher against the pod's memory.

- 2026-11-14, Run B rerun: I edited the launcher (`followup2_pod.sh`) before its harness had the new scenarios, so the
  first harness run could not show that the new scenarios fail on the old code. Mitigation: a red run of the new harness
  against the installed old launcher (`results/pods/logs_harness/f2_harness_red.log`) before the new launcher is
  installed. Guard (written rule): for a launcher change, install nothing until a red harness log against the installed
  copy exists; the review brief names that log, and a brief without it is not sent.
- 2026-11-14, Run B rerun: the worker check named in the guard above is a fixed count (7, from the Mac peak of 2.39 GB
  per cell, `memprobe/rss.log`) and a launcher refusal outside 1 to 16, not a live check of the pod's memory.
